section.subsection:
In an administrative garnishment order issued under this section, the commission shall:

identify the taxpayer, including:
the taxpayer's name and address; and
if known:

the last four digits of the taxpayer's social security number, or the taxpayer's full social security number, if the taxpayer's full social security number is required by federal law; and
the taxpayer's date of birth;
contain a statement that includes:
if known, the nature, location, account number, and estimated value of the property subject to administrative garnishment;
if known, the name, address, and phone number of the person holding the property subject to administrative garnishment; and
the name, address, and phone number of any person claiming an interest in the property described in Subsection (7)(b)(i) or (ii);
state whether any of the property subject to administrative garnishment consists of earnings;
state the outstanding amount owed under the warrant described in Subsection (3)(a);
state the amount of any applicable costs or fees included in the administrative garnishment;
state the manner in which the garnishee shall deliver the property to the commission; and
state that the commission shall pay the garnishee the fee described in Section 78A-2-216.

As part of the administrative garnishment order, the commission shall serve on the garnishee the following interrogatories:

whether the garnishee is indebted to the taxpayer and, if so, the nature of the indebtedness;
whether the garnishee possesses or controls any property of the taxpayer, and, if so, the nature, location, and estimated value of the property;
whether the garnishee knows of any property of the taxpayer in the possession or control of another person, and if so, the following information about the property:
the nature;
the location; and
the estimated value;
whether the garnishee intends to deduct from the property a liquidated claim against the taxpayer;
a description of any claim described in Subsection (8)(d)(i); and
the amount deducted, if any;
the date and manner of the garnishee's service of the documents described in Subsection (9)(c) on the taxpayer and any third party;
the date on which the taxpayer was previously served with any continuing administrative garnishment order;
any other relevant information the commission requests, including:
the taxpayer's position;
the taxpayer's rate of pay;
the taxpayer's compensation method;
the taxpayer's pay period; and
a computation of the taxpayer's disposable earnings.

subsection.subsection:
A continuing administrative garnishment order applies to payments to the taxpayer:
beginning on the day on which the continuing administrative garnishment order is served; and
ending on the earlier of:

subject to Subsection (15)(c), one year after the day on which the continuing administrative garnishment order is served;
120 days after the day on which a second or subsequent continuing administrative garnishment against the taxpayer is served;
the day on which the last nonexempt periodic payment subject to the continuing administrative garnishment order occurs;
the day on which the warrant described in Subsection (3)(a) is stayed, vacated, or satisfied in full; or
the day on which the commission releases the continuing administrative garnishment order.
